Fix gnu_inline attribute error in cfns.h

When building GCC 4.7.2 with modern GCC, there's a conflict with the
gnu_inline attribute. The function declaration at line 57 needs to match
the function definition at line 132 which includes __attribute__((__gnu_inline__)).

This fixes the error:
cfns.gperf:101:1: error: 'gnu_inline' attribute present on 'libc_name_p'
cfns.gperf:26:14: error: but not here

Signed-off-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/gcc/cp/cfns.h
+++ b/gcc/cp/cfns.h
@@ -53,6 +53,9 @@ static unsigned int hash (const char *, unsigned int);
 static unsigned int hash (const char *, unsigned int);
 #ifdef __GNUC__
 __inline
+#ifdef __GNUC_STDC_INLINE__
+__attribute__ ((__gnu_inline__))
+#endif
 #endif
 const char * libc_name_p (const char *, unsigned int);
 /* maximum key range = 391, duplicates = 0 */
